   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1342-opus, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 379ba4052cb36894ba2b53ccf049ab9a6f2ab204\n\n1. **Medium, PR #1342 body (no `### Ledger` section).** This PR fixes a defect shared with legacy (`Common.swift:3212` @ 87fe0d1c), but the body has no `### Ledger` section. Under AGENTS §8, the steward will fold nothing, so `CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` will never record the change. The other #866 HIG fixes did record theirs (rows 1254 and 1263). Fix: add a `changelog` block. UX section, a French summary (« Page numéro » : la feuille peut s'agrandir (`.medium`) et défile aux grandes tailles de texte), `#1167`, `HFRswift/Swift/Common.swift:3212` @ `87fe0d1c`.\n2. **Low, `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderPageSheet.swift:58-60`.** The `// Port of … Differences:` header does not mention the new difference from legacy (extra `.medium` detent plus `ScrollView`), which AGENTS §4 requires. Fix: add one clause citing #1167.\n3. **Low, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/ReaderPageSheetDetentsTests.swift:8`.** The test only compares the constant with a copy of its own literal. If you remove the `ScrollView`, or put `[.height(260)]` back in the view, it stays green; without the change it fails only because it doesn't compile (L01). Fix: either say in the PR that the Mac check on #893 is what verifies this, or test something the view actually depends on.\n4. **Detail, `ReaderPageSheet.swift:6`.** The comment \"`.medium` lets the sheet grow when Dynamic Type…\" reads as if the sheet grows by itself. It doesn't: at AX sizes it still opens at 260 pt (the smallest detent), and the user has to scroll or drag. That's acceptable under the issue (\"visible or scrollable\"). If you want it to grow by itself, the issue's alternative works: `presentationDetents(_:selection:)` starting at `.medium` when `dynamicTypeSize.isAccessibilitySize`. Separately, the AX5 Mac check should also look at sideways truncation of the four `-10…+10` buttons, which a vertical `ScrollView` can't fix.\n\nNo other problems found: `PresentationDetent` is `Hashable` and `Sendable`; `presentationDetents(Set)` is fine, `.scrollBounceBehavior` needs iOS 16.4, below the app's minimum; `navigationTitle` and `toolbar` are still attached inside the `NavigationStack`; the only call site (`TopicReaderView.swift:143-149`) sets no other presentation modifier; the cited legacy line is correct.\n\n**Verified:** diff, issue #1167, the legacy source at `87fe0d1c:HFRswift/Swift/Common.swift:3212`, every use of `ReaderPageSheet`, `ReaderPagePicker` and `presentationDetents`; `swiftlint lint --strict` on both changed files clean; `check_legacy_pointers.py --fetch` at the head: 0 wrong. Not built: no Xcode in this session.\n\nRound 1 fixed in 7d0d123 and in the PR body: `### Ledger` `changelog` row added (checked with `ledger.py check-body`) (1); header names the difference (2); the PR and the test now say the Mac check is what verifies the opening height, the scrolling and the drag (3); the comment says the sheet opens at 260 pt and is dragged taller, opening at `.medium` by itself is listed as not done, and the AX5 Mac check now covers the sideways truncation of the four buttons (4). Round 2 requested.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
