   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1342-opus-r2, round 2) : APPROVE** — head 7d0d123\n\nRound 1 findings, checked again on this head:\n- **Ledger:** the PR body has a `### Ledger` section with one `changelog` row in section UX. It parses: `ledger.py check-body --pr 1342 --file <body>` gives \"1 block(s) ok\".\n- **`// Port of` header:** it now names the difference, a second detent and scrolling content that legacy's fixed 260 pt lacks.\n- **Test:** the PR and the test's doc comment both say it only pins the detents value. The real behaviour at AX3/AX5 is left to the Mac check.\n- **Legacy citation:** `Common.swift:3212` @ 87fe0d1c is `.presentationDetents([.height(260)])`, read with `git show`.\n\nInitial height: with a `Set` and no selection binding, the sheet should open at the smallest detent. On the smallest iPhone in portrait, `.medium` is taller than 260 pt, so the sheet still opens at legacy's height. I could not build or run it here; the Mac check covers this.\n\nFindings:\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderPageSheet.swift:101`. The comment \"at a large text size it grows or scrolls\" still suggests the sheet grows by itself. In fact the member drags it to `.medium`, as the doc comment on `detents` and the PR body correctly say. Fix: \"…the member can drag it taller, and the content scrolls meanwhile\".\n2. **Detail**, process. The PR body says a Mac check is owed on #893, but #893 has no comment naming #1167 or #1342 yet. Fix: once merged, add it to #893 as the to-do of AGENTS §7 (\"Host\").\n\n**Checked**: the diff against `origin/dev-swift` in a worktree at 7d0d123; `swiftlint lint --strict` on both changed files: 0 violations; `check_legacy_pointers.py --fetch`: 0 wrong; `ledger.py check-body`: ok; issue #1167: the acceptance criteria are met by `[.height(260), .medium]` plus the `ScrollView`; the legacy line at 87fe0d1c; the only call site is `TopicReaderView.swift:145`. Not built and tests not run: no Xcode in this cloud session.\n\nAuthor's answer, comment only: finding 1 applied in f349f5d (the comment now says the member drags the sheet taller; the line was wrapped for the 140-column limit, `swiftlint lint --strict` clean). Finding 2: the Mac check is on #893 with the ready line of this PR. The delta after the reviewed head is two comment lines.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
